WEBVTT

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:31.786
So Alex has been experimenting
with unstructured interaction

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.576
to create shared understanding.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:35.906
AC: We've definitely done virtual lunches.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:40.106
I think one of the things
that is missing most instantly

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.307
when you go full remote

00:17:41.331 --> 00:17:45.146
is the sort of just camaraderie
associated with being able

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.146
to just kind of have a
conversation about nothing

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.406
around the lunch table,

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:52.633
and it's weird to set a meeting and say,

00:17:52.657 --> 00:17:55.309
"The agenda is we're not
going to talk about work,

00:17:55.333 --> 00:17:57.069
and everybody please have fun."

00:17:57.093 --> 00:17:59.253
It's like that is, that's a weird agenda.

00:17:59.277 --> 00:18:01.376
It's hard to do.